WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.550
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.160
Before this duel ends, I 
want to hear the true story.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.790
What happened ten years ago?

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.990
It’s called the "Lost Incident."

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.460
Six children went missing one-by-one.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.840
I have the right to know what 
the incident's mission was.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.360
To heal the wounds in my heart, 
I received treatment for years.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.110
But no matter how much time passed…

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.720
I couldn't forget.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.940
I investigated the incident 
and found something.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.830
The Lost Incident had another 
name: Hanoi Project!

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:53.300
The name of Hanoi Project’s 
mastermind is in this data.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.650
Who is it?

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.820
I run Across the universe

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.990
At the speed of light

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.860
Begin Loading

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.590
Open the door of dreams

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.160
VRAINS spreads

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.270
Believe in myself

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.800
VRAINS continues

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:40.110
The circuit draws the future

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:44.180
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.780
Access!

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.480
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.090
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.390
Link with my soul

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.160
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.890
Now Win the Race

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.730
Connected world

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.230
No matter when

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.600
Nothing is impossible

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.740
Strive for hope

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:15.310
And ride the wind!

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.560
Who is it?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.890
Answer me, Zaizen!

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:57.370
I can’t tell you.  What's the point?

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:02.840
It'll only increase your hatred, 
turning you into the devil of revenge.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.840
It must end here!

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.140
Hmm…

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:14.340
Playmaker, you two are on parallel tracks.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.260
Seems so.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.110
Our opinions match for the first time!

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.460
I’m touched!

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.690
I guess I have to stop you here.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.920
Go ahead and try.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.340
The goddess of victory is on my side.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.600
Resume the duel!

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.400
My turn!  I draw!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.070
I'll finish you this turn!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.880
This is the final attack!  Battle!

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.740
Tindangle Acute Cerberus, attack Firewall!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.880
Acute Math Blaze!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:04:00.370
Due to Morley's Shield and Nagel's 
Protection’s effects, Tindangle monsters are invincible.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:05.680
If Gergonne's End's conditions 
are met, Playmaker will lose.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.970
Even if they aren't, if 
Playmaker takes this attack...

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:13.300
...the damage doubling effect 
will erase all his LP.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.770
It's over, Playmaker!

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.440
What are you going to do, Playmaker?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.690
Just be quiet.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.720
You should be panicking more!

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.250
The Quick-Play Spell, Cynet Backdoor!

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.910
By banishing a Cyberse on my field...

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:36.560
...I can add a Cyberse in my 
deck with lower ATK to my hand.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:42.560
The banished monster returns 
to my field on my next turn.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.090
And it can attack you directly.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.800
I banish Firewall Dragon!

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:53.910
I add Draconnet from my deck to my hand.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:59.180
Hey!  If you banish Firewall, 
his attack will come towards us!

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:03.480
No.  Since Doppler Phase Coating 
is no longer equipped...

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.920
...it goes to the graveyard, 
and its effect activates.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:12.330
When this card leaves the field during 
the Battle Phase, the Battle Phase ends!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.290
What?

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.540
You just might survive!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.510
He changed the situation with just one card?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:30.750
When the banished Firewall Dragon returns to 
the field next turn, it can attack directly.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.040
If that happens, Playmaker wins.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.830
It'll be a huge comeback!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.530
But Acute Cerberus’s effect!

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:44.770
When the battle ends, you can 
Special Summon a Tindangle Token.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.730
Due to Tindangle Acute Cerberus’s effect...

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:55.280
...it gains 500 ATK for every 
monster it’s linked to.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.250
What he’s doing is pointless!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:06.680
No matter how high he raises 
its ATK, it’s over next turn!

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.580
You think so?

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.660
I can make a comeback too!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:16.420
I activate the Field Spell, Euler's Circuit!

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.460
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.930
What?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.380
What’s this?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.480
What is this?

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:44.590
When he has at least three Tindangles on 
his field, your monsters can’t attack.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:45.990
What?

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.850
And once during his Standby Phase...

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:55.560
...he can move his Tindangle and place 
it next to Acute Cerberus’s link.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.940
He can move it to our field?

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.770
My brother has Acute Cerberus 
and two Tindangle Tokens.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:08.340
So Playmaker can’t attack.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.080
On Akira’s next turn...

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:15.680
...if he fills all of Acute 
Cerberus’s links...

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:21.050
...Gergonne's End will deal 
4500 damage to Playmaker.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:23.610
Another comeback.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.790
It seems Akira will win this duel.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.800
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:37.150
Sorry to bother you, but I 
need to pack up for my move.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:41.150
Damn!  Can nothing be done?

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:43.740
Good good good.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.110
That’s right, Zaizen.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.110
Don’t give him that data!

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.440
SOL Technologies’ secret...

00:07:52.440 --> 00:08:00.020
If I get it, I'll have a trump card 
to use against the higher-ups!

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:03.930
That'll help me get a promotion.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:10.200
Zaizen, fight hard for my promotion!

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:15.440
Zaizen, this is a duel for justice.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.920
Yes, I know.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:21.150
That’s why I must win.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:26.520
I'll solve this incident and 
hold the people responsible!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.490
No, you don’t know anything.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:35.700
I'll win because this is a duel for justice!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.260
What?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:41.980
I don’t trust anything but my own justice!

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.400
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:47.640
Cynet Backdoor’s effect!

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:52.440
The banished Firewall Dragon 
returns to my field!

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.890
Next, I summon Draconnet!

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.050
Draconnet’s effect activates!

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:09.290
When it's summoned, I can Special Summon

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:14.470
a Level 2 or lower monster from my 
hand or deck in defense position!

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:18.000
I Special Summon Bitron from 
my deck in defense position!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.440
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.280
I set Bitron in the Link Marker!

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.720
Link Summon!

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.190
Appear!

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:38.140
Link 1 Link Spider!

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.630
What’s the point of summoning it now?

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:46.110
Link Spider’s effect activates!

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:53.850
Once per turn, I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower monster from my hand next to its link.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:57.090
I Special Summon Digitron from my hand!

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:04.280
Appear again!  The circuit 
that leads to the future!

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.520
Another Link Summon?

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:09.490
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:13.500
I set Digitron and Draconnet 
in the Link Markers!

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.300
Link Summon!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:21.170
Appear, Link 2 Recovery Sorcerer!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:26.600
Appear for a third time!  The 
circuit that leads to the future!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.580
Triple Link Summon?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.410
No matter how many you 
summon, it’s pointless!

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:36.310
As long as Euler's Circuit envelops 
the field, you can’t attack!

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:39.150
We know that!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:44.240
But we just wanted to 
show off before we lose-

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.490
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.870
The summoning condition is 
one Cyberse Link Monster!

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:52.210
I set Link Spider in the Link Marker!

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:55.070
Circuit combine!

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.800
Link Summon!

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.710
Appear, Link 1 Security Gardna!

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.810
This card can’t be used to Link Summon.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:10.860
And only one Security Gardna can 
be faceup on my field at a time.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:15.300
I place Security Gardna on the field… here!

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:19.670
That position is…

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:22.400
Hey, what are you thinking?

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.870
That’s next to the scary pooch's link!

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:30.860
He did three Link Summons 
in a row, but he burned out.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:35.880
He summoned a monster next to Acute Cerberus.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.370
He knew that he couldn't win, 
so he chose self-destruction.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.960
As you wish, I'll end this duel!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:48.350
The trap card Gergonne's 
End’s effect activates!

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:53.420
When the equipped monster has 
monsters next to all its links...

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:56.600
...by destroying those monsters 
and Gergonne's End...

00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:00.320
...the opponent takes damage equal 
to the equipped monster’s ATK.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:07.110
I destroy two Tindangle Tokens, 
Security Gardna and Gergonne's End!

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:12.310
You take damage equal to 
Acute Cerberus’s ATK.

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:16.060
Go, Tindangle Acute Cerberus!

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.080
Playmaker…

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:32.920
Lost?

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:38.280
Playmaker, your revenge is over.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.940
Are you sure?

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.410
Ta daa!  We’re fine!

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.200
No way!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.620
Gergonne's End's effect should've...

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.640
But we didn't take the effect!

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:05.500
When Security Gardna is Special Summoned, 
effect damage becomes 0 that turn.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:08.610
It negated the effect damage to me!

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:11.340
Security Gardna has that effect?

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.940
You fell for it!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.270
We did it, Playmaker!

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:23.320
See that?  He was fooled 
by my excellent acting!

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:29.190
Due to your horrible acting, he 
almost realized what I was up to.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:35.910
I won't win the acting award for Best AI.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:41.240
Acute Cerberus is linked to fewer 
monsters, so it loses 1000 ATK.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:48.370
And since there are fewer Tindangles on your 
field, Euler's Circuit’s effect ends.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.640
So I can attack!

00:13:52.490 --> 00:14:00.580
Since Cynet Backdoor allows Firewall Dragon 
to attack you directly, you’re finished.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:03.800
Recovery Sorcerer’s effect!

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:08.030
Since a co-linked Cyberse Link 
Monster was destroyed this turn...

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:13.970
...I can Special Summon a destroyed Link 
Monster once by negating its effects.

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.940
Resurrect, Security Gardna!

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.360
Hey, what are you doing?

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:26.010
He has a scary pooch, but 
you can attack him directly!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.620
A duel isn’t just for 
deciding a winner and a loser.

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.290
Firewall Dragon’s effect!

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:38.000
For every monster that’s 
co-linked with this card...

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:43.400
...I can return a monster on our fields 
or graveyards to our hands once!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.000
Emergency Escape!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.910
Two monsters are co-linked 
with Firewall Dragon.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:56.210
So I return Tindangle Hound and Tindangle 
Angel from your graveyard to your hand.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:05.780
When Tindangle Hound or Tindangle 
Angel are in the graveyard...

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:09.260
...Acute Cerberus gains 
1500 ATK for each one.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:14.730
Since they’re now both gone from 
your graveyard, it has 0 ATK!

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.560
Battle!

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.520
Firewall Dragon!

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.330
Attack Tindangle Acute Cerberus!

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:30.080
Tempest Attack!

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.360
Brother!

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.360
Brother...

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.200
I’m fine.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.300
Impressive, Playmaker.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.280
To make a comeback from that situation.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:04.510
No one may be able to erase 
his fire for revenge anymore.

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.520
As promised, I'm taking the data.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.230
Ai, eat as much as you want.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:23.480
Playmaker, what did you just say?

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.240
Did you say my name?

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.390
Hurry up.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:28.230
Okay okay.  Sheesh.

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.680
Leave it to me!

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:36.350
I’ll eat everything!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.660
I ate a lot.  I’m stuffed.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:57.400
Zaizen, stay away from 
the incident and from me.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.630
Playmaker!

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:05.340
If your Firewall attacked me directly 
earlier, you would’ve won.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.440
So why?

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:15.850
Tindangle Hound and Tindangle Angel 
have the power to protect each other.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.920
They represent you two.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:24.400
You two shouldn’t be 
resting in the graveyard.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:28.770
My revenge shouldn't drag 
you into the darkness.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:33.400
You should walk where there's light.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:40.950
Everyone, bye bAi!  Get it?

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:46.600
Time for me to leave too.

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.760
Be nice to each other.

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:56.100
In the end, I couldn’t do anything.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:59.080
That's not true.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:04.890
At the very least, I now 
understand how you feel.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:11.280
And no matter who tries to stop 
him, he'll walk his own path.

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:14.730
Just like how you tried to protect me.

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.640
That’s what I think.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.200
Aoi…

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:25.400
Zaizen, you’re worthless!

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:32.560
How could you allow Playmaker 
to steal our company’s data!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:38.180
If others find out, I'll no 
longer be Security Manager!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:41.560
No one must find out!

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:43.460
No one!  No one at all!

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:45.540
And no one must ask!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.280
I think I hear something.

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:50.280
Me too.

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:53.510
Playmaker stole the data.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:02.260
I wonder who'll buy this 
data at a high price?

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:16.140
Are you okay, Yusaku?

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.220
Kusanagi…

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.480
Well done.

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.900
All thanks to me!

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.020
Yeah.  You did great too.

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:27.300
Hooray!  He praised me!

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:28.660
Hooray!  Yeah!

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:32.370
Kusanagi, analyze it immediately.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.500
Sure.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.460
You’re gonna look at 
my private parts again?

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:41.240
Be quiet or I’ll turn off the speaker.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.210
Okay.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.160
Let me see…

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:48.890
A file about the incident 
should be somewhere.

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:53.130
Kusanagi!  This one!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:59.130
Dr. Kogami.  Kiyoshi Kogami.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.840
Planned and executed the Hanoi Project.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.840
He’s the Hanoi Project’s mastermind?

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.450
What does it say?

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:08.820
This man is…

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:13.800
A researcher at SOL Technologies.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.380
You don't seem surprised.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:19.300
I expected this.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:23.350
That’s why SOL Technologies had this info.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:28.020
It says that Dr. Kogami 
caused the incident alone.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:32.780
But SOL Technologies found 
out due to a whistleblower.

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.780
Alone?  Really?

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:38.950
Maybe Zaizen was involved?

